  "evidence_boundary": "On 57 fully exposed development cases, a gold-aware offline lexical oracle found a single source-line span reaching official F1 0.45 in 48 cases, while Qwen3.5:27b still missed that threshold in 40 of those cases. Thirty-nine of the 40 misses were carried by the session Time line and 38 were temporal questions. Only 6 of 48 oracle passes had F1 1.0; the other 42 were partial-F1 spans, so semantic answer sufficiency and a selector fix remain unproven. This localizes the observed metric gap to temporal source-anchor use, composition, or answer expression and authorizes only a separately preregistered source-disjoint deterministic temporal/span mechanism; gold-aware runtime use, fresh generation, full-pipeline work, runtime change, shadow mode, and production remain unauthorized."
